  "scientific_diagnosis": "The empirical findings confirm a severe score-distribution calibration shift on cartoon and sketch. While ROC-AUC remains high (0.84 - 0.90) across all domains, the logit scores for cartoon and sketch are shifted downwards by 1.5 to 2.5 logit units relative to photo. Consequently, a photo-calibrated threshold (tau=1.1413) fails to trigger on cartoons (TPR 2.8%) and sketches (TPR 0.3%). When domain-aware recalibration is applied, TPR recovers to 18-35% at 1% FPR. However, because this requires labelled domain data at deployment time, the manuscript retains the uncalibrated numbers as the primary benchmark."
